# narrative_events.md.backup

This sanitized brief outlines the Narrative Events system without referencing project-specific storylines.

## Core Concepts

- Branching story hooks react to player alignment, chapter progression, faction standing, boss outcomes, and global world state changes.
- Triggers are defined through data files so designers can add or disable events without code changes.

## Event Categories

- Intro sequences that set context for a run.
- Dynamic events that appear mid-session.
- Hub interactions that evolve between missions.
- Chapter-specific beats that reflect long-term progress.
- Reputation moments tied to major factions or player choices.

## System Outcomes

- Unlocking new powers or modifiers.
- Adjusting faction reputation and alignment meters.
- Updating saved world-state variables that other systems consume.

## Implementation Notes

- Narrative events expose hooks for UI prompts, audio cues, and optional rewards.
- Persistence is handled via the Save System so that choices carry between sessions.
- Designers should avoid embedding sensitive narrative text in configuration files; store localized strings in separate assets.
